The iPXE script a Forge instance boots. Rendered by BuildForgeNodePayloads and
sent as NicoMachineTemplate.spec.template.spec.ipxeScript.

Both URLs are inputs rather than constants: which OS image boots is the whole
point of qualifying one, so pinning a build here would mean every run qualified
the same image regardless of what it was asked to qualify.

Everything below the URLs is the boot configuration the hardware needs and
does not vary per run. The amd64 console and kernel parameters are kept
verbatim from controller/hack/create-forge-nico-cluster.sh, the one path known
to have booted a node on this site.

The arm64 line is likewise verbatim from machines known to have booted: the
GB200 nodes of the 2026-09-29 site-2 run, Forge instances
ffdc0d8f-34b8-48d3-95ca-4add9c688bb9 (site controller) and
8afe358d-66d2-45f0-b2e9-b1552d41a5b2 (tenant GPU worker), read back from
GET /v2/org/<org>/forge/instance/<id>.

Do not derive it from the amd64 line. Three of its parameters do not follow:
intel_iommu=on names a controller no ARM machine has and is absent, iommu=pt is
spelled the same rather than as iommu.passthrough=1, and pci=realloc=off is
present despite reading as x86-only. ip=dhcp and fb=false appear on this
hardware and nowhere else. The arm64 release fixture in
controller/test/fixtures disagrees with all of this, and is not evidence here:
it describes a virtual machine under nico-sim, not a Grace node.

The same goes for luks-key, which those instances do not set. The amd64 line
passes luks.key=changeit and boots the non-FDE image anyway, so the parameter
is evidently tolerated there, but nothing here has booted an arm64 node with
it. Qualifying an arm64 FDE image will need a key, and this is where it goes.
*/ -}}
#!ipxe
set boot-loader {{ .BootLoaderURL }}
set image-url {{ .ImageURL }}
set disk-strategy smallest

{{ if eq .Arch "arm64" -}}
set console-config console=ttyAMA0,115200
set kernel-params ip=dhcp fb=false pci=realloc=off loglevel=1 iommu=pt
set luks-key
{{- else -}}
set console-config console=tty0 console=ttyS1,115200
set kernel-params pci=realloc=off reboot=pci loglevel=1 iommu=pt intel_iommu=on
set luks-key luks.key=changeit
{{- end }}
set cloud-init-ds ds=nocloud-net;s=${cloudinit-url}

chain ${boot-loader} ${console-config} ${kernel-params} ${luks-key} image_url=${image-url} disk_strategy=${disk-strategy} ${cloud-init-ds} update_grub_template=yes update_grub_cfg=yes
boot
